  "name": "Gray-Scott Niches: heredity",
  "description": "The heredity test with Gray-Scott Niches: four walled circles, each seeded with one species (spots, worms, maze, curly), each living on its own food and competing only for space (interfere 0.3). Open doors with the Unwall tool (key 8). In the lab, doors opened at 30k: by 150k spots and worms still held about 11–13% of their own circles (in Gray-Scott Species they die out), but maze and curly, which fill space faster, took the rest of every circle and the ground between, about 55/45. The territory slider (each species' food dip harming the others) made it worse in the lab: curly took everything but the maze circle. Tint = local mean feed; view b1…b4 to see one species.",
